 \section{Interpretation and limitations}
 The arithmetic can prevent a reporting overclaim, but it cannot tell an investigator which events are useful, what distance is being traversed, how activity relates to mobility, or how much entropy is produced. Those are empirical and model-selection questions. Heterogeneous event weights, signed progress, reserve events that also advance the endpoint, continuous time, stochastic dependence, state-dependent mobility, and measurement error all lie outside the model.
